-- title:
--   First special-fibre component of X₁(Mp) is an Igusa model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M\ge 5$ with $M\neq 0$ and $p\nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ equal to the $L$-subfield generated by the image of the coefficientwise map $L((q)) \supseteq$ $\mathbb{Q}((q))$-subfield $x1FunctionFieldC\ \mathbb{Q}\ (Mp)$ under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), i.e. the base change to $L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$; let $j\in K$ be nonzero with $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (that is, $q^{-1}$ times the power series $jNumQ$, coefficients pushed to $L$), and let $X = TwoChartModel\ A\ K\ j$ with its structure morphism [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ that is an $A$-algebra. Let $C_1,C_2$ be schemes with morphisms $c_1, c_2$ to $\operatorname{Spec} k$ that are proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and let $i_1, i_2$ be morphisms from $C_1, C_2$ to the geometric special fibre $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} k$ (the second pullback projection being its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} k$) which are closed immersions and commute with the structure morphisms, such that every point of the fibre lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, the scheme-theoretic intersection $C_1\times_{X_k} C_2$ is reduced, and its cardinality equals $n$ with $n>0$. Let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2$ sections of $c_1,c_2$, with $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ equal to the base change of $\varepsilon$ to $k$. Finally let $w$ be an integral weight-one form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $k$: a modular form of weight $1$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with an integral power series that is its $q$-expansion and whose reduction-type invariant $intSeriesC\ k$ is nonzero. The conclusion is that there exist a curve model $Mdl$ over $k$ of the Igusa function field $igusaFunctionFieldX1C\ k\ M\ w \subseteq k((q))$ — an integral scheme with a proper morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} k$ smooth of relative dimension $1$, a ring isomorphism of that field with the function field of the scheme compatible with the structure map from $k$, a bijection between closed points and places of the field under which stalks correspond to valuation subrings, and such that every finite set of points lies in an affine open — and an isomorphism $e : Mdl.C \cong C_1$ with $e$ followed by $c_1$ equal to the structure morphism of $Mdl$.
--
--   This is the statement that the first of the two components of the geometric special fibre at $p$ of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ is the smooth proper $k$-curve attached to the Igusa function field in characteristic $p$ (Katz–Mazur 13.11, Edixhoven §6); it is one conjunct of the corresponding two-component statement and is also used in the version recording the Gauss-reading normalisation of the first component.
